00:15:00,612 --> 00:15:02,012
Market's going up, going up, going up.

234
00:15:02,112 --> 00:15:04,512
Okay, you're seeing these aggressive buyers here.

235
00:15:04,512 --> 00:15:09,012
You've got a big buying imbalance right up here near the high, which is what you want to see.

236
00:15:09,512 --> 00:15:10,212
That's normal.

237
00:15:11,112 --> 00:15:13,912
You're expecting to see a lot of buying happening near the high.

238
00:15:14,212 --> 00:15:15,669
People are expecting the market to

239
00:15:15,669 --> 00:15:16,640
go higher, and it

240
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:19,311
does. It pops right back up. It hits a new high.

241
00:15:19,312 --> 00:15:20,384
You've got a divergence

242
00:15:20,384 --> 00:15:22,528
up there. Which is a sign to say,

243
00:15:22,528 --> 00:15:26,012
ooh, okay, you hit a new high, but you got a negative delta.

244
00:15:26,412 --> 00:15:28,612
So obviously selling came in right at the high.

245
00:15:29,012 --> 00:15:33,212
And then immediately after, you're getting aggressive selling. You get a stacked selling imbalance.

246
00:15:34,512 --> 00:15:36,612
And what happens? The market falls right over.

247
00:15:36,812 --> 00:15:44,512
You hit the high. And you see in the order flow, first you got your divergence.

248
00:15:45,412 --> 00:15:50,812
You hit the new high, but where's the rest of the buying? The selling overtook the buying in that bar.

249
00:15:51,212 --> 00:15:53,712
And then in the next bar, you got a stack selling imbalance.

250
00:15:54,212 --> 00:15:56,190
where there's a lot of sellers coming

251
00:15:56,190 --> 00:16:00,711
in and kicking off a bunch of selling imbalances, and the market just sold right off.

252
00:16:03,412 --> 00:16:07,212
Again, you've seen this chart a lot in the earlier lessons.

253
00:16:07,912 --> 00:16:09,012
But it's a perfect example.

254
00:16:09,112 --> 00:16:11,012
Okay, this is S&Ps at 1940.

255
00:16:12,712 --> 00:16:15,712
You know, we worked our way up, hit the high.

256
00:16:16,012 --> 00:16:17,512
You got big stopping volume up here.

257
00:16:17,512 --> 00:16:19,912
In 1940, you got 1,600 lots traded there.

258
00:16:20,812 --> 00:16:22,112
The market couldn't get past it.

259
00:16:22,112 --> 00:16:25,512
You know, there's obviously somebody with big supply there.

260
00:16:26,212 --> 00:16:30,612
And, you know, the market came off, you know, slightly before it. You know, you have a small print.

261
00:16:30,912 --> 00:16:33,012
Immediately after it, again, you got a small print.

262
00:16:33,712 --> 00:16:36,312
The market did try to go back up. It couldn't take off the high.

263
00:16:36,512 --> 00:16:40,812
You know, you get selling of balances right up near the top of the bars.

264
00:16:41,412 --> 00:16:45,112
And, you know, the markets are just, it just sells right off.

265
00:16:45,712 --> 00:16:48,712
You know, why isn't the market, you know, keep going up?

266
00:16:48,712 --> 00:16:52,212
Well, you can see you have this big volume here.

267
00:16:52,612 --> 00:16:55,812
You know, you got to always be asking yourself, what's going on in the market?

268
00:16:57,912 --> 00:17:00,516
When you see things that are not

269
00:17:00,516 --> 00:17:03,120
normal, when you see big volumes that

270
00:17:03,120 --> 00:17:07,212
end the moves and the market can't get past it, why?

271
00:17:07,612 --> 00:17:08,312
What's happening?

272
00:17:08,612 --> 00:17:09,412
There's a shift.

273
00:17:09,912 --> 00:17:12,212
Obviously, there's somebody with a lot of supply to sell.

274
00:17:15,512 --> 00:17:23,312
Basically saying to all the buyers that want to try and take it higher, sure, I'll sell whatever you want.

275
00:17:23,712 --> 00:17:24,412
How much do you want?

276
00:17:24,912 --> 00:17:25,612
I'll sell it to you.

277
00:17:26,112 --> 00:17:26,812
No problem.

278
00:17:30,012 --> 00:17:32,712
You know, again, this is similar.

279
00:17:32,712 --> 00:17:35,712
You know, you're working your way up. Work, work, work.

280
00:17:35,812 --> 00:17:37,212
You know, positive deltas.

281
00:17:37,312 --> 00:17:40,112
You know, even this bar, it's a red candle. It's still got positive delta.

282
00:17:40,212 --> 00:17:41,812
So, you know, there's still a good buying in there.

283
00:17:43,512 --> 00:17:45,612
Right up here near the high, you've got a buying imbalance.

284
00:17:45,612 --> 00:17:48,012
You know, you're just, you know, two ticks off the high.

285
00:17:48,112 --> 00:17:48,812
It squirts up.

286
00:17:49,412 --> 00:17:51,012
You know, you make a new high.

287
00:17:51,912 --> 00:17:52,812
Well, what happens?

288
00:17:53,812 --> 00:17:54,912
You got a divergence.

289
00:17:55,212 --> 00:17:56,112
Sellers came in.

290
00:17:56,512 --> 00:18:02,912
Even, okay, you will forgive this bar. The next bar, again, the sellers have come in.

291
00:18:03,412 --> 00:18:05,512
Okay, so you're not yet convinced.

292
00:18:06,712 --> 00:18:08,362
This third bar you have here,

293
00:18:08,362 --> 00:18:13,312
you got a ratio, a single print, and you got a bunch of selling imbalances in the bar.

294
00:18:13,712 --> 00:18:19,412
I mean, if you didn't really notice it in the second bar, in this third bar, it's really quite obvious.

295
00:18:21,412 --> 00:18:25,612
So you have to ask yourself, why isn't the market going higher?

296
00:18:25,712 --> 00:18:30,512
You see this nice buying imbalance. Where is the follow-through? It's not there.

297
00:18:31,212 --> 00:18:37,612
And all of a sudden, you see the big shift in delta where the sellers are taking over.

298
00:18:40,700 --> 00:18:44,500
It's something that order flows will really help you see.

299
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:48,080
Sometimes it's very obvious, like in

300
00:18:48,080 --> 00:18:50,260
this case, other times it does

301
00:18:50,260 --> 00:18:52,440
take a little bit of work

302
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:56,800
to understand it, but over time you'll understand it a lot clearer.

303
00:18:58,800 --> 00:19:02,600
So this is a move, as it's happening, it's going straight up.

304
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:10,800
Understanding the order flow will help you catch moves like this.

305
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:18,800
You see the point controls all starting, each one subsequently higher, acting as support for the previous bar.

306
00:19:19,600 --> 00:19:21,000
The deltas are all positive.

307
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,300
You're seeing single prints.

308
00:19:24,300 --> 00:19:29,100
On the way up, which is helping to indicate to you that the market is starting to pull away.

309
00:19:30,900 --> 00:19:36,800
Earlier, the market was just sort of in this area here, in a little bit of a range.

310
00:19:37,300 --> 00:19:40,271
But now you're starting to see heavy volume

311
00:19:40,271 --> 00:19:45,099
on the bid side. Which is indicating that there's support in the market.

312
00:19:45,300 --> 00:19:46,578
Even though the market's going up,

313
00:19:46,578 --> 00:19:47,856
people are trying to sell into

314
00:19:47,856 --> 00:19:50,199
the bid to pull it back down, push it back down.

315
00:19:50,300 --> 00:19:52,000
You've got 1,000 traded here.

316
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:56,000
You've got 765 here, 500, 400.

317
00:19:57,500 --> 00:20:02,400
And the market's moving up. It's moving up nicely without much resistance.

318
00:20:02,600 --> 00:20:06,400
You're seeing only a few hundred being traded on the offer on the way up.

319
00:20:08,100 --> 00:20:13,000
Size here, 826 is the biggest amount that's traded on the move up. Here you got 1,200.

320
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:17,400
It's the path of least resistance.

321
00:20:18,100 --> 00:20:23,100
The buyers are taking it up. And it's not on thin volume. It's decent volume.

322
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:30,000
Each bar is 5,000, 3,000, 4,000, 3,000, 5,000.

323
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:32,800
People are interested in moving the market.

324
00:20:33,100 --> 00:20:37,200
Somebody is buying it up. Accumulating a position nicely.

325
00:20:37,200 --> 00:20:44,800
They're not necessarily overpowering the market and just buying it up immediately. It's happening over a period of time.

326
00:20:45,400 --> 00:20:52,500
This is 1036 up to 1040. It's a five minutes, but it's a nice move from 1880 basically up to 1890.

327
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:54,900
It's a nice gradual move.

328
00:20:55,200 --> 00:20:57,100
These are the types of moves that you want to catch.

329
00:21:01,688 --> 00:21:02,521
Okay, so, you

330
00:21:02,521 --> 00:21:03,909
know, this is a, again,

331
00:21:03,909 --> 00:21:05,575
this is an E-mini chart. And,

332
00:21:05,575 --> 00:21:09,186
you know, come back up, come off a little bit, come back up.

333
00:21:09,188 --> 00:21:10,848
You often see that with,

334
00:21:10,848 --> 00:21:12,508
you know, just a normal

335
00:21:12,508 --> 00:21:14,168
trading day, you know, where

336
00:21:14,168 --> 00:21:17,488
the market's just sort of bing, bing, bing, bing around.

337
00:21:18,088 --> 00:21:23,188
And, you know... What you want to do is you want to catch this move up.

338
00:21:23,188 --> 00:21:28,488
You're seeing on the move up, you're seeing some early buying imbalances. You don't necessarily see them later.

339
00:21:29,688 --> 00:21:31,160
Then you're starting to see the

340
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:35,085
selling imbalances come in, a couple more buying imbalances as you push a little bit higher.

341
00:21:35,188 --> 00:21:36,454
Then the selling imbalances,

342
00:21:36,454 --> 00:21:38,354
you've got three here, one here,

343
00:21:38,354 --> 00:21:40,254
two here, I'm sorry, three here,

344
00:21:40,254 --> 00:21:42,787
one here, as the market moves back down.

345
00:21:43,088 --> 00:21:45,388
You're not seeing any more buying come in.

346
00:21:45,988 --> 00:21:48,388
To a lesser extent, after you hit this high,

347
00:21:49,388 --> 00:21:57,088
You got this bar here with three selling imbalances and a couple of selling imbalances either side of it.

348
00:21:58,488 --> 00:21:59,074
And, you know,

349
00:21:59,074 --> 00:22:00,051
the market did come back

350
00:22:00,051 --> 00:22:02,787
up a little bit. You know, it took out the high of this bar.

351
00:22:03,488 --> 00:22:06,688
And, you know, slightly before it, you got a few buying imbalances.

352
00:22:07,288 --> 00:22:08,688
But what happens?

353
00:22:08,688 --> 00:22:10,638
It shifts, and then you're starting

354
00:22:10,638 --> 00:22:12,588
to see the selling imbalances come

355
00:22:12,588 --> 00:22:16,488
in on the way down, which is what you want to see.

356
00:22:16,988 --> 00:22:19,349
Here, you thought it was going to happen

357
00:22:19,349 --> 00:22:23,187
a little bit early, but the buying came in. You can see that.

358
00:22:23,588 --> 00:22:24,352
So, you know, had

359
00:22:24,352 --> 00:22:25,116
you gotten short here,

360
00:22:25,116 --> 00:22:25,880
you know, and you

361
00:22:25,880 --> 00:22:26,835
have to stop, you know,

362
00:22:26,835 --> 00:22:30,083
here, you could... just sort of see that, you know, okay, maybe it's not happening right now.

363
00:22:30,088 --> 00:22:32,888
You could get out at a little bit of a scratch or a loss.

364
00:22:33,288 --> 00:22:37,239
But then, you know, again, when it starts to happen, you know,

365
00:22:37,239 --> 00:22:43,825
it's literally around the same price, and you catch the move, you know, from 1904 down to, you know, 1899 or lower.

366
00:22:45,988 --> 00:22:48,888
I mean, that's what order flows will tell you.

367
00:22:49,188 --> 00:22:53,888
They'll tell you the different types of trading that's happening in the market.

368
00:22:54,088 --> 00:22:57,116
When people are being aggressive in the sense

369
00:22:57,116 --> 00:23:00,144
that they're overwhelming the other side of the

370
00:23:00,144 --> 00:23:04,686
market, you tend to see that with the imbalances as they're occurring.

371
00:23:05,388 --> 00:23:10,788
When the market is going sideways, it's really hard to get a gauge on the market.

372
00:23:10,788 --> 00:23:18,688
But once the market starts moving, order flows will help you determine the intensity of the move.

373
00:23:19,188 --> 00:23:24,388
If you're starting to see a lot of imbalances come in as the market starts moving away,

374
00:23:24,788 --> 00:23:28,288
from a high or a low, you know, that's important.

375
00:23:28,388 --> 00:23:29,888
You know, that's where you're going to make money on.

376
00:23:30,888 --> 00:23:31,760
That's, you know,

377
00:23:31,760 --> 00:23:33,795
that's the value that exists in order

378
00:23:33,795 --> 00:23:37,284
flow that you're not going to see on a regular bar chart.

379
00:23:38,988 --> 00:23:43,788
And I can't stress it enough, you know, order flows allows you to see, you know,

380
00:23:44,188 --> 00:23:49,688
the intensity of a move that you just can't see in a candlestick chart or a bar chart by itself.

381
00:23:51,588 --> 00:23:52,170
So, you

382
00:23:52,170 --> 00:23:53,043
know, anyway, that's

383
00:23:53,043 --> 00:23:55,081
the end of lesson six, you know,

384
00:23:55,081 --> 00:23:58,284
the different types of trading that's happening. happening in the market.

385
00:23:58,288 --> 00:24:03,188
In the next lesson, I'll explain the best futures markets to trade order flow.

386
00:24:03,188 --> 00:24:03,631
You know,

387
00:24:03,631 --> 00:24:04,961
a lot of people are asking,

388
00:24:04,961 --> 00:24:06,291
what's the best market to trade

389
00:24:06,291 --> 00:24:08,286
order flow? There really is no one best market.

390
00:24:08,288 --> 00:24:11,788
I'll discuss many of the markets that you can trade.

391
00:24:12,188 --> 00:24:15,488
Basically, any market out there, you can trade as long as it's a

392
00:24:16,888 --> 00:24:23,988
Something that trades with a decent amount of volume on an intraday basis, order flow can be applied to it.

393
00:24:24,488 --> 00:24:27,895
I trade a wide range of contracts from

394
00:24:27,895 --> 00:24:30,876
grains to financials to a lesser extent

395
00:24:30,876 --> 00:24:35,987
currencies, but a lot of commodities, things that follow supply and demand.

396
00:24:36,588 --> 00:24:38,988
Supply and demand is a law, it's not a theory.

397
00:24:42,288 --> 00:24:45,151
Laws that apply to supply and demand

398
00:24:45,151 --> 00:24:51,287
in the wheat market also apply to supply and demand in the index futures markets.

399
00:24:51,388 --> 00:24:57,288
So in the next lesson, I'll explain the different types of markets that you can trade.

400
00:24:57,788 --> 00:25:03,888
Is anyone better? It really depends on your risk tolerance and the time you have to devote to trading.

